<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/13th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dudenev's raid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1293">1293</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dudenev's raid was a punitive campaign by an army of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-horde">Golden Horde</a> under the commander Dudenev (<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duden">Duden</a>), sent by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokhta">Tokhta</a> Khan in 1293 at the request of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/andrei-of-gorodets">Andrei of Gorodets</a> against his brother, Grand Prince <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dmitry-of-pereslavl">Dmitry of Pereslavl</a>. The army sacked Vladimir, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suzdal">Suzdal</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolomna">Kolomna</a> and some fourteen other towns of north-eastern Rus'. Dmitry fled, and Andrei received the grand principality.</p></div>
